<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>local.ollama.env</string>
  <!--
    Ollama.app spawns its own server as a child process, so it never reads
    ~/.zshrc. GUI apps inherit the launchd user session environment instead,
    which only `launchctl setenv` can populate. This agent seeds it at login;
    Ollama.app must be restarted afterwards to pick up new values.

    The settings keep a 23GB model from crowding out the rest of the machine:
      KEEP_ALIVE         unload after 2 min idle (default 5m)
      MAX_LOADED_MODELS  never hold two models resident at once
      NUM_PARALLEL       1 - the default allocates KV cache per parallel slot
      KV_CACHE_TYPE      q8_0 KV cache, roughly halves cache memory
      FLASH_ATTENTION    required for KV cache quantisation to take effect

    Two settings are absent because the environment cannot reach them. The app
    keeps its own copy in the `settings` table of
    `~/Library/Application Support/Ollama/db.sqlite` and hands those to the
    server, beating anything set here. Both were confirmed by restarting the app
    with the variable set and reading back the `server config` line in
    ~/.ollama/logs/server.log. Change them in the app's own settings UI:

      context_length   OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH loses to this. Left alone: the
                       app's 131072 costs only ~1.4GB over the 21.7GB of
                       qwen3.6:35b-a3b-coding weights, because a q8_0 cache on
                       a 3B-active MoE is small.
      expose           OLLAMA_HOST loses to this. Ships as 0, but at 1 the
                       server binds 0.0.0.0 and the whole LAN reaches an API
                       with no authentication, where /api/delete and /api/pull
                       are as open as /api/chat. Keep it off unless something
                       off-host genuinely needs the model, which a container
                       would, since host.docker.internal resolves to the
                       gateway address rather than to loopback.
  -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/sh</string>
    <string>-c</string>
    <string>launchctl setenv OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE 120; launchctl setenv OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS 1; launchctl setenv OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL 1; launchctl setenv OLLAMA_FLASH_ATTENTION 1; launchctl setenv OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE q8_0</string>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
